# Data conversion between megabyte and petabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between megabyte and petabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MB to 0.0000PB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0000PB; backward, converting 1PB to 1000000000MB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PB yields 1500000000.0MB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MB
print(forward_whole->to(PB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(forward_fractional->to(PB))
backward_whole: int = 1PB
print(backward_whole->to(MB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(backward_fractional->to(MB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PB
0.0000PB
1000000000MB
1500000000.0MB

<<< stderr
